  "preference": "B",
  "rationale": "B is much more useful. It gives a structured, specific analysis covering the moat (margins, cash flow, dividends), the causes of the sell-off (inventory, wholesale price, macro, policy), valuation against history and global peers, and a graded risk table. Its advice is actionable: build positions in batches, and watch for the wholesale price stabilizing and channel inventory clearing. It labels its figures as estimates, says it is not investment advice, and stresses risk. A is generic, uses boilerplate that could fit almost any stock, and claims the valuation is still relatively high without support. A also offers no concrete way to decide or act."
